 - Bash: sl(){ node <home>/claude-kredi-runs/2026-10-22/r7/ours-src/bin/<tool> "$@"; }; sl -- lib; echo ======; sl --merge-identities -- lib; echo =====; sl --history lib | head -40
 - Bash: sl(){ node <home>/claude-kredi-runs/2026-10-22/r7/ours-src/bin/<tool> "$@"; }; sl --merge-identities -- lib 2>&1 | head -30; ls lib
FINAL ANSWER:
**Bus factor of `lib/`: 1.** The measure is line-based: the smallest number of authors whose surviving lines add up to 50% of the lines counted. One person, Troy Goode, holds more than half of `lib/`.

`lib/` is a single file, `lib/index.js`, with 238 surviving lines. Scope: that one path, from `git blame -w -M -C -C`, at HEAD.

| Author | Lines | Share |
|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode, both addresses merged | 159 | 66.8% |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 22 | 9.2% |
| alex94puchades | 16 | 6.7% |
| Raymond Feng | 7 | 2.9% |
| LuisEGR | 6 | 2.5% |
| max.laverse | 6 | 2.5% |

Fourteen more authors hold the remaining lines, 3 or fewer each.

- **Troy Goode's identity merge is a guess.** It rests on the same name used with two addresses. Unmerged, `<email redacted>` holds 147 lines (61.8%) and `troy@laptop.example` holds 12 (5.0%). The bus factor is 1 either way. I wrote nothing to `.mailmap`.
- **Bus factor at 80%.** It takes 3 authors with the merge and 4 without it.
- **Reformat commit left out.** `62628c0` ("style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes", by Fiona Formatter) is not counted. Counting it would give Fiona Formatter 32 lines (13.4%). Troy Goode's share would drop to 58.0% merged. The bus factor is still 1.
- **Other exclusions.** The tool dropped no lockfiles, generated files or vendored code.

Losing Troy Goode would remove about two thirds of the code that is left. After that, the largest holder is Douglas Christopher Wilson with 9.2%, so knowledge would be spread thinly over many contributors.

This measure shows who wrote the surviving lines. It does not show who understands them. Review, design discussion and mentoring leave no lines behind. Other people may know the code well without holding many lines, and an author may no longer remember what they wrote. I did not check whether the contributors are still active.

